Passed (the R2 check was already in). Now criterion 5: R3 exact times at 10:15:30 → codigo C (6 chars), trocaEm = 10:16:00-03:00, validoAte = 10:17:00-03:00.

This is the test that verifies the rotation math concretely. The implementation already computes trocaEm/validoAte. This test mostly verifies exact values. Whatever code C is, I compare instantes. Note: codigo is deterministic but any 6-char value satisfies the criterion (the criterion says "código C" — meaning a specific code, but we can't know it beforehand; assert 6 chars). The key assertions: trocaEm and validoAte exact instants.

Let me write:

```ts
it("R3 - às 10:15:30 o código pertence à janela 10:15:00, com trocaEm 10:16:00 e validoAte 10:17:00", async () => {
  await resetar("2026-10-19T10:15:30-03:00");
  const r = await fetchJson("/encontros/enc_5e6f7a8b/codigo", { headers: { "X-Usuario": "org-ana" } });
  assert.equal(r.status, 200);
  const body = r.body as { codigo: string; trocaEm: string; validoAte: string };
  assert.match(body.codigo, /^[A-Z0-9]{6}$/);
  assert.equal(new Date(body.trocaEm).toISOString(), new Date("2026-10-19T10:16:00-03:00").toISOString());
  assert.equal(new Date(body.validoAte).toISOString(), new Date("2026-10-19T10:17:00-03:00").toISOString());
});
```

Run.

